  "schema_version": 1,
  "status": "candidate-built",
  "stream_interior": "Stream-only organic interior. Let S(t)=clamp(t,0,1)^2*(3-2*clamp(t,0,1)), E=S((minimum signed polygon-edge distance-8)/8), A=2pi(x/142+y/80), B=2pi(x/142-y/80), using world x/y. Warp local route lookup by E*(1.2*sin(A),1.2*sin(B)); core radius=width/2+0.8*E*sin(A+0.4)*cos(B). Thus the 8-world-pixel edge zone is unchanged and the envelope reaches full effect at 16 px. For junctions, smoothly union core SDF with a central disc of radius 0.68*width at warped coordinates: h=max(3-abs(core-disc),0)/3, merged=min(core,disc)-3*h*h/4, core=core+E*(merged-core). Border=max(0,border-0.8*E+0.3*E*sin(B+0.7)). Pocket=S((sin(A)*sin(B)-0.15)/0.65); bank opacity=1-0.65*E*pocket; final alpha=outer_AA*(core_AA+(1-core_AA)*bank_opacity). Cores stay opaque; translucent earth banks reveal underlying terrain with no baked-in grass. Road arithmetic and protected stream profiles are unchanged.",
  "texture_method": "New opaque source images only. Bilinear source sampling through continuous mirror-periodic coordinates, periods (142,80); average f(x,y) and f(x+71,y+40) in byte RGB. This derived texture average is invariant under all six lattice neighbor shifts. All independent cells use world origin phase (0,0). No original-game pixels.",
